Both halves of the shared root — the `at` carry and the harnessVersion carry —
are pinned by a biting mutant. That is the coverage that matters: a future edit
to noTurnProbe itself cannot pass silently. FINDINGS 1 and 3 CLOSED at the root.

M7 is an EQUIVALENT MUTANT, not a coverage gap, and I say so rather than
counting it. `NEVER_PROBED_AT = ""` is unparseable, so `priorAtMs` maps it to
-Infinity; a fixed old parseable date sorts first too, for every timestamp this
studio will ever produce, so no observable ordering changes. The two differ only
in honesty, not behaviour: an unparseable sentinel says "no evidence time",
whereas a fabricated date is exactly the alternative the brief refuses by name
("*Zero a stranded pair's `at`*: it makes the record lie about when the pair was
last seen"). Asserting the sentinel's literal value would test the
implementation rather than the behaviour. No action.

